     "I have a small problem using Stefan&#39;s exact.matches function.<br><br>When I introduce the following line:<br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:13px;line-height:17px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.3\"><span style=\"color:blue\">matches.ficar&lt;-exact.matches(&quot;\\\\bfic(a|á|o)(|s|r|mos|m|u|ste|ram)&quot;, sarptg, lines.around = 2)</span></pre></span></span><br>The output generates tabs around  the first part of the regex only, as in:<br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:13px;line-height:17px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.3\">sempre\\tfica\\tram longe<br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:13px;line-height:17px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.3\">hospitais\\tfica\\tm  <br><br><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Is this a problem in the function itself or did I formulate my regex wrongly? <br><br>Thanks for your comments!<br><br>cv <br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"></span></pre></span></span><br></pre></span></span>"
